{
  "body_human_readable": "The Oklahoma City Thunder won the 2024-2025 NBA season championship, defeating the Indiana Pacers in a seven-game series. This marks the franchise's first title since relocating to Oklahoma City and their second overall, the first being in 1979 as the Seattle SuperSonics.\n\nThe Thunder emerged victorious in a decisive Game 7 with a score of 103-91. The Finals concluded on June 22, 2025.\n\nKey Performers:\n*   **Finals MVP:** Shai Gilgeous-Alexander of the Oklahoma City Thunder was named the NBA Finals Most Valuable Player.\n*   **Regular Season Record:** The Thunder held the league's best regular-season record at 68-14.\n*   **Leading Scorer:** Shai Gilgeous-Alexander also led the league in scoring during the season.",
